      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lemon Springs began as a mineral spring resort in 1890, founded by industrialist John W., drawing visitors for picnics and dances.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lemon_springs_north_carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "dropped_surname_no_wiki_source"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town blossomed along the Raleigh & Augusta Air‑Line Railroad, serving as a major depot for tobacco farmers arriving in the 1910s and 1920s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lemon_springs_north_carolina",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Lemon House, a log and frame dwelling built around 1853, exemplifies Scotch‑Irish and German architectural styles in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lemon_springs_north_carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Lemon Springs Home Demonstration Club, founded in 1920, is the county’s oldest civic group and now operates the Extension and Community Association.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lemon_springs_north_carolina",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Located at roughly 390 feet elevation in the Carolina Sandhills, Lemon Springs sits on well‑drained Tertiary sands that shape its landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lemon_springs_north_carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lemon Springs enjoys a humid subtropical climate, averaging 61°F annually and offering about 200 frost‑free days that support local farming.",
